# Veyra — Product Context (source of truth)

Full document: `docs/VEYRA_CONTEXT.md` (also in `veyra/docs/VEYRA_CONTEXT.md`).

## North star

> **Veyra is the identity agent for the physical world.**

```text
Presence → Identity → Authorization → Action
```

Veyra is **not** primarily a payment terminal. Palm payment is the first PoC use case — not the product limit.

Credentials (palm first; face/voice later) → **Veyra ID** → policy/risk → **Action** (PAY, ACCESS, CHECK-IN, VERIFY, ATTENDANCE, CUSTOM).

## Abstractions providers (never couple domain)

- Biometrics behind `BiometricDevice` (first Chinese palm reader is replaceable)
- Payments behind `PaymentProvider` (Stripe first; Adyen/Conekta later)
- Voice behind abstraction (ElevenLabs preferred for experiments)
- Realtime/agent UI inspired by LiveKit Agents UI — not domain core

## First PoC loop

```text
Demo POS → $10 MXN → Veyra Terminal → ✋ → Veyra ID → PSP → APPROVED → POS PAID
```

Prove `Palm → Veyra ID → Authorized Action` before payment coupling. Milestones M0–M5 in context doc. Agent UI/voice only after action state machine is reliable.

## Surfaces

Consumer app · Terminal (states: IDLE→…→SPEAKING→COMPLETE) · Merchant Console · Platform · SDK/API (`POST /v1/actions`).

## Commercial model (working hypothesis — not final)

**Hardware-as-a-Service + recurring subscription + usage/transaction economics.**

| Plan | Activation | Subscription | Notes |
|------|------------|--------------|-------|
| Start | ~MXN $1,499 | ~MXN $499/mo | Standalone device |
| Business | ~MXN $999 | ~MXN $799/mo | POS integration |
| Enterprise | Custom | Custom | API/SDK/OEM |

Hardware ref cost ~MXN $4,200. Do not scale inventory before PoC/unit economics. $300/mo alone is too low for payback.

Other revenue: activation, rental/comodato, per-tx / bps, PSP share, per verify/access, enterprise.

## Landing / brand UX direction

- Formal biometric trust (not playful fintech gimmicks)
- Show **palm reader + voice agent** together (terminal agent states, ambient visualizer)
- Visual references: [ElevenLabs](https://elevenlabs.io/) (clean, dark, professional) + [LiveKit Agents UI](https://livekit.com/products/agents-ui) (listening/speaking/thinking)
- Spanish B2B copy for Mexico operators
- Preserve modular monolith direction; inspect before large refactors

## Execution rule

Read `docs/VEYRA_CONTEXT.md` before major product/architecture work. Prefer smallest increment to prove the loop. Wait for approval before large refactors outside explicitly requested surfaces (e.g. landing redesign).
